    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Kingsville-TX/Adjunct-Faculty--Communications_R-082607": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty, Communications Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department Department Of Art, Comm, & Theatre Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Job Summary The Art, Communications, and Theatre (ACT) Department at Texas A&M University-Kingsville is accepting applications for part-time lecturers in speech communications. On-campus and dual enrollment courses across the south Texas region are possible assignments.  Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate lower-level speech communications courses as needed by the Department. Minimum Qualifications Masters degree with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in the field of communications from a regionally accredited institution or university. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching public speaking at the university level. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Kingsville-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice--Communication-Sciences---Disorders_R-089692-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice, Communication Sciences & Disorders",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-12-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Practice, Communication Sciences & Disorders Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department Department of Clinical Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Clinical Health Sciences is seeking an experienced Clinical Instructor to join our accredited program in Communication Sciences & Disorders at Texas A & M University-Kingsville.  We are located in historic Kingsville, TX home of the legendary King Ranch and Kingsville- Naval Air Station. Our South Texas location is near the Gulf coast - Corpus Christi area, with beaches, birding, and fishing. For more information about the university please visit our website at http://www.tamuk.edu/about/index.html   The rank, Assistant Professor of Practice, is for a 9-month non-tenure track position with summer teaching possible/optional. The successful applicant will be expected to supervise/instruct graduate student clinicians in the on-campus clinic and possibly some local community outreaches, teach courses in the undergraduate and/or graduate program in CSDO and provide service to the university and profession.   Minimum Qualifications:    ·       Texas SLP Licensure or eligible to obtain Texas Licensure   ·       Certificate of Clinical Competence (CCC) in Speech-Language Pathology  ·       Three years of experience post CCC  ·       MS or MA in Communication Sciences & Disorders    Consideration will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.   Salary is commensurate with qualifications. Consideration of applications begins immediately and continues until a suitable candidate is identified.  To apply go to https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUK_External .  Please submit letter of application, curriculum vita, copies of transcripts, and three original letters of recommendations electronically. You may also contact Maura Krestar, Ph.D., Chair of Department of Clinical Health Sciences, Communication Sciences and Disorders at Texas A&M University-Kingsville, 700 University Blvd, MSC 177A, Kingsville, TX 78363, phone 361-593-3404 or email Maura.krestar@tamuk.edu.  Note that prior to issuing a letter of appointment, official transcripts must be received directly from each degree granting institution by the Office of the Provost, Texas A & M University- Kingsville, MSC 102, Kingsville, Texas 78363-8202.  However, for review of application, applicants may submit unofficial transcripts from each institution of higher education attended directly to the search committee. Note: If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator (AACRAO). Selected candidate must pass a pre-employment background investigation to be hired for this position.   Texas A & M University-Kingsville is committed to excellence; the University invites applications from all qualified applicants.  All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Kingsville-TX/Adjunct-Faculty--English_R-088384-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty- English",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-10-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty- English Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department Department of Language & Literature Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Job Summary Adjunct in English (non-tenure track), beginning Spring 2026. Responsibilities Will teach one to five sections per fall/spring semesters. Courses include first-year composition and sophomore literature at the undergraduate level. Minimum Requirements (1) Minimum earned 18 graduate credit hours in English or related field or a master’s degrees in English or related field from a regionally accredited institution or university. (2) Teaching experience in person, hybrid, and/or online course delivery. (3) Experience with students desirable. (4) Demonstrated history of quality teaching is expected. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Kingsville-TX/Adjunct-Faculty--Studio-Art-and-Art-History_R-082441": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Studio Art and Art History",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty, Studio Art and Art History Agency Texas A&M University - Kingsville Department Department Of Art, Comm, & Theatre Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Kingsville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Job Summary The Art, Communications, and Theatre (ACT) Department at Texas A&M University-Kingsville is accepting applications for Dual Enrollment Lecturers in Art History and Studio Courses.  Dual Enrollment courses across the Coastal Bend & South Texas region are possible assignments.   Lecturer will teach lower level Art Courses as needed by the department.  Art History classes will be taught as needed.   Studio Art courses will be taught in Kingsville on campus. Minimum Requirements A Master's degree in the field of Art from a regionally accredited institution or university.  Must have a minimum of 18 graduate hours for each field that they teach.   Experience teaching Art History and/or Studio Art courses at the university level.   Prior to issuing a letter of appointment, official transcripts must be received directly from each degree-granting institution by the Office of the Provost, Texas A&M University-Kingsville, MSC 102, Kingsville, Texas 78363-8202.  However, for review of the application, applicants must submit unofficial transcripts from each institution of higher education attended within their application. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator (AACRAO): http://www.aacrao.org/international/foreignEdCred.cfm   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    }
  },
